+for what the operation costs. `walletFeesNanograms` stays the root wallet
+transaction fee F, and the preview reports `operationSpendNanograms`, what
+the wallet spends beyond the values: with send mode +1 (pay fees separately:
+modes 3 and 19, and the mode-less default) F plus the part of the forwarding
+fee that travels with the message, and for modes 2 and 18, whose values pay
+the forwarding fee, F less the action fee. Such a preview succeeds only with a
+known spend and only when the values plus the spend fit the balance; equality
+fits, and one nanogram less is `InsufficientBalanceForFees` with the fee and
+the spend. When the wallet skipped every message, a zero-value companion
+emulated at the same block prices them, and the preview is the funds refusal
+with that fee and spend, or `EmulationRejected` where the spend fits. A
+refusal that established no amount carries none, and an unknown spend is never
+zero. Messages of one intent must share a fee kind for a spend to be known.
 
